+These results establish a claim about exploration and nothing more. Across the three systems the launch policy reached states and transitions that fixed restart rules and generated ensembles did not, at budgets one to three orders of magnitude below the corresponding references. The pooled frames come from a launch distribution that changes every epoch, so they are not samples of the stationary distribution. The cell-level weighting used for the trypsin networks maps occupancies onto the fitted transition model; it does not establish equilibrium populations or remove unresolved within-cell sampling effects. Validated populations, free energies, and rates require estimators whose assumptions are checked independently, so we report state discovery, committor orderings, and model-derived network connectivity instead.
